WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.048
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.318 --> 00:54.284
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
01:33.531 --> 01:36.075
Wait. We're not done talking.

4
01:43.917 --> 01:44.751
What?

5
02:12.654 --> 02:14.447
Father, stay inside!

6
02:34.801 --> 02:35.843
It's from the bathroom.

7
02:36.928 --> 02:38.012
Stay back.

8
02:45.728 --> 02:47.105
You, get out of the way!

9
03:19.262 --> 03:20.722
It's not me.

10
03:22.265 --> 03:23.099
Move!

11
04:01.429 --> 04:02.555
Hands in the air.

12
04:16.027 --> 04:16.944
Hands up!

13
04:30.750 --> 04:32.043
Open it now!

14
04:32.126 --> 04:33.378
Break the door!

15
04:34.253 --> 04:35.338
Open it already!

16
04:48.684 --> 04:50.728
Father, stay there!

17
05:06.911 --> 05:09.080
Make one wrong move, and I'll shoot.

18
05:55.501 --> 05:56.878
Get him! He's the killer!

19
06:38.294 --> 06:40.421
So-ran, are you okay?

20
07:07.990 --> 07:09.033
Mr. Suzuki.

21
07:11.744 --> 07:12.578
Mr. Suzuki?

22
07:15.164 --> 07:16.082
Mr. Suzuki.

23
07:17.917 --> 07:19.710
Father! Are you all right?

24
07:58.374 --> 08:03.504
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

25
08:03.588 --> 08:05.881
EPISODE 2

26
08:46.589 --> 08:47.882
Are you one of them?

27
08:48.924 --> 08:50.968
Where did he run off to? Say it!

28
08:52.678 --> 08:54.889
I had nothing to do with it, I swear!

29
09:01.729 --> 09:04.649
But first, I have something to tell you.

30
09:09.362 --> 09:11.155
Honey.

31
09:15.576 --> 09:16.410
Honey?

32
09:17.828 --> 09:18.704
What is it?

33
09:18.788 --> 09:21.332
Are you going to prove that you're not involved?

34
09:22.249 --> 09:23.751
Yes, I can prove it.

35
09:26.295 --> 09:27.588
That maid isn't one of them.

36
09:36.514 --> 09:39.809
When the killer brought her to the bathroom as a hostage,

37
09:39.892 --> 09:41.852
she warned me of an assassination.

38
09:42.603 --> 09:44.355
Thanks to her, I could act quickly.

39
09:46.607 --> 09:48.275
In other words, it was her

40
09:48.359 --> 09:50.069
who saved me and my father.

41
09:50.695 --> 09:51.737
By the way, Chief.

42
09:52.947 --> 09:55.282
How did he even get past security?

43
09:59.870 --> 10:00.746
Take her.

44
10:01.539 --> 10:03.207
I have something to tell you…

45
10:03.290 --> 10:04.709
I have something to tell you!

46
10:04.792 --> 10:07.128
Honey.

47
10:07.878 --> 10:08.713
Honey.

48
10:10.840 --> 10:12.341
We need to lay her down now.

49
10:14.093 --> 10:15.553
Help me, Seo-hee.

50
10:17.096 --> 10:18.889
Keum Seo-hee!

51
10:28.691 --> 10:29.525
Yes, ma'am!

52
10:29.608 --> 10:30.526
Freeze!

53
10:38.659 --> 10:40.619
Are you going to take responsibility for this?

54
10:45.166 --> 10:47.752
If anything happens to my wife and my baby…

55
10:52.339 --> 10:57.511
I'll hold the Government-General accountable through the U.S. Consulate.

56
11:13.569 --> 11:14.403
Let her go.

57
11:38.344 --> 11:39.345
Think carefully.

58
11:40.221 --> 11:42.473
Saying useless things now isn't going to help you.

59
11:42.556 --> 11:44.934
If you want your 60 won, you'd better cooperate.

60
11:47.186 --> 11:48.020
I know.

61
11:48.938 --> 11:50.189
That's why I'm here.

62
11:52.942 --> 11:53.776
But…

63
11:54.610 --> 11:56.403
I think you owe me 100 won.

64
11:56.487 --> 11:57.988
I nearly got killed too.

65
12:08.791 --> 12:09.667
Put the guns down!

66
12:13.337 --> 12:15.172
Why were you hiding a gun?

67
12:15.923 --> 12:19.885
With things so dangerous these days, it's for self-defense.

68
12:21.846 --> 12:23.138
I already had it on me

69
12:23.681 --> 12:26.559
when the police searched me before dinner.

70
12:28.978 --> 12:31.564
Mr. Yoo Philip fired the gun at the killer,

71
12:32.648 --> 12:33.482
but he missed.

72
12:34.650 --> 12:37.236
If you keep suspecting us,

73
12:37.319 --> 12:40.489
I'll have no choice but to write about what happened tonight.

74
12:42.199 --> 12:46.662
Someone tried to assassinate the new inspector general.

75
12:47.288 --> 12:51.292
Could the killer be someone opposed to Japan's rule of Joseon?

76
12:52.042 --> 12:53.419
If news like this gets out,

77
12:53.502 --> 12:55.588
what will the world think of Japan?

78
12:55.671 --> 12:57.089
The international community

79
12:57.172 --> 12:59.884
is already watching Japan because of Manchukuo.

80
13:04.096 --> 13:07.308
I can personally vouch for our maid's identity.

81
13:07.850 --> 13:10.436
Don't lay a hand on her again

82
13:10.519 --> 13:12.229
and stop suspecting her.

83
13:14.356 --> 13:17.276
Consider this a warning.

84
13:18.903 --> 13:19.778
Chief!

85
13:21.822 --> 13:22.907
Did you find him?

86
13:22.990 --> 13:23.824
Yes, sir.

87
13:26.619 --> 13:28.621
He's the cake deliveryman from Itsukoshi.

88
13:28.704 --> 13:30.581
He was knocked out on a delivery.

89
13:30.664 --> 13:33.584
When he woke up, his uniform and bike were gone.

90
13:34.376 --> 13:35.252
Are you sure?

91
13:35.336 --> 13:37.880
I swear it's true. I'm not lying!

92
14:00.027 --> 14:02.446
I hope your wife feels better soon.

93
15:00.212 --> 15:02.715
Do you have any idea what you've done?

94
15:04.591 --> 15:05.676
I have…

95
15:07.136 --> 15:09.888
waited so long for this day.

96
15:09.972 --> 15:11.140
You just…

97
15:11.724 --> 15:14.852
destroyed everything I've ever lived for!

98
15:17.396 --> 15:18.230
Well…

99
15:19.023 --> 15:20.482
I mean…

100
15:20.566 --> 15:24.153
This wouldn't have happened if you'd just paid me earlier.

101
15:24.236 --> 15:26.447
Money?

102
15:27.364 --> 15:30.868
You ruined everything over a little money. Are you happy now?

103
15:30.951 --> 15:34.705
Do you even realize what you've done for that stupid money?

104
15:35.414 --> 15:37.332
Don't blame me.

105
15:37.416 --> 15:39.043
I nearly died myself.

106
15:44.965 --> 15:46.425
Just give me the money you promised.

107
15:51.972 --> 15:53.974
Bring me the bullets first.

108
15:58.353 --> 16:00.272
Seriously, I knew it.

109
16:02.691 --> 16:04.860
Forget it. I'll just sell them myself.

110
16:04.943 --> 16:06.695
Seriously, though,

111
16:06.779 --> 16:08.947
I would have brought you the bullets if you'd paid me.

112
16:09.531 --> 16:12.576
But whatever. It's no big deal. I can do without it.

113
16:12.659 --> 16:14.286
It's no big deal?

114
16:14.369 --> 16:17.748
Yeah. I never imagined I'd get involved in the independence movement

115
16:17.831 --> 16:19.917
and nearly die over a little money.

116
16:20.834 --> 16:22.377
So forget the money.

117
16:22.878 --> 16:25.547
Good luck with the independence movement. Don't fail next time.

118
16:25.631 --> 16:27.466
Don't you care about your own country?

119
16:29.426 --> 16:31.678
Why does everyone keep saying the same thing?

120
16:33.013 --> 16:33.972
Look.

121
16:34.515 --> 16:37.351
I was born into a country already under Japanese rule.

122
16:37.434 --> 16:38.936
Is that my fault?

123
16:39.019 --> 16:41.021
You can't blame me, can you?

124
16:41.105 --> 16:43.649
Am I supposed to fight for independence just because I was born in Joseon?

125
16:45.943 --> 16:47.694
What has Joseon ever done for me?

126
16:53.909 --> 16:55.536
You want to fire a gun here?

127
16:56.662 --> 16:58.372
The police are still outside.

128
17:00.958 --> 17:02.918
I'm not a snitch.

129
17:03.502 --> 17:06.046
I already told them I'm the live-in maid here.

130
17:06.130 --> 17:08.132
If you get caught, do you think I'll be safe?

131
17:12.052 --> 17:14.930
There's no way we'll see each other again.

132
17:15.514 --> 17:16.890
Believe me, I deeply regret

133
17:17.766 --> 17:19.643
ever setting foot in this house.

134
17:24.898 --> 17:26.024
Let her go.

135
17:28.402 --> 17:29.236
So-ran.

136
17:29.319 --> 17:31.989
Today's operation has already fallen through.

137
17:32.072 --> 17:32.906
Still, if--

138
17:32.990 --> 17:35.325
Besides, she has a point.

139
17:44.960 --> 17:47.546
If you stole anything, give it back before you go.

140
17:47.629 --> 17:48.839
Stole something?

141
17:49.882 --> 17:51.258
What are you talking about?

142
17:51.341 --> 17:52.759
Should I search you?

143
18:05.397 --> 18:06.231
Happy now?

144
18:07.441 --> 18:09.610
I was going to switch the photo and go to America.

145
18:09.693 --> 18:10.527
America?

146
18:10.611 --> 18:13.780
Yes, I'm saving up so I can go to America.

147
18:14.907 --> 18:16.116
You can't go there.

148
18:17.159 --> 18:19.077
They won't take you in.

149
18:20.162 --> 18:20.996
What?

150
18:21.079 --> 18:22.956
I said you can't go to America.

151
18:23.665 --> 18:26.126
If you don't believe me, ask the U.S. Consulate.

152
18:26.210 --> 18:28.420
Do you realize you're being so childish?

153
18:42.309 --> 18:43.810
So-ran, are you okay?

154
18:44.436 --> 18:45.604
Are you hurt anywhere?

155
18:47.272 --> 18:48.148
No, I'm fine.

156
18:50.692 --> 18:53.820
Thanks to you shooting him, we're in the clear for now.

157
18:55.530 --> 18:59.034
I think he's an independence fighter, but I have no idea where he came from.

158
18:59.117 --> 19:01.495
The Provisional Government knows we're trying to kill Sato,

159
19:01.578 --> 19:02.955
so I doubt he's with them.

160
19:08.418 --> 19:10.295
His name is Keum Seok-jung.

161
19:14.716 --> 19:15.634
Do you know him?

162
19:18.136 --> 19:20.973
For 13 years, I didn't know if he was alive or dead.

163
19:24.017 --> 19:27.604
I wanted nothing more than to find him and kill him.

164
19:34.361 --> 19:35.779
He's my husband.

165
20:10.522 --> 20:11.398
You.

166
20:12.065 --> 20:14.026
Are you really the maid here?

167
20:14.901 --> 20:16.903
Enough with the lies. Tell me the truth.

168
20:17.487 --> 20:19.239
Who are you really, Keum Seo-hee?

169
20:19.948 --> 20:22.409
I am the live-in maid here. You heard that earlier.

170
20:22.492 --> 20:23.869
Stop lying.

171
20:23.952 --> 20:26.246
If that's true, why were you in first class?

172
20:26.330 --> 20:27.539
And what about today?

173
20:28.415 --> 20:30.876
I've never heard of a live-in maid who speaks English.

174
20:30.959 --> 20:32.669
I'll take that as a compliment.

175
20:32.753 --> 20:35.047
I couldn't go to school, so I couldn't get any other job.

176
20:35.130 --> 20:36.757
But that's not my fault, is it?

177
20:37.257 --> 20:39.634
If you're really the live-in maid here,

178
20:39.718 --> 20:41.595
what are you doing outside now?

179
20:41.678 --> 20:42.721
The house is a mess.

180
20:42.804 --> 20:44.973
You should be cleaning or tending to the madam.

181
20:45.057 --> 20:47.934
I'm out getting medicine for her.

182
20:48.018 --> 20:49.394
As you know,

183
20:49.478 --> 20:52.022
she's not feeling great after what happened earlier.

184
20:52.105 --> 20:54.524
So would you mind letting me through? I need to go.

185
20:54.608 --> 20:56.068
If you keep suspecting me,

186
20:56.151 --> 20:57.986
I'll tell the inspector general.

187
20:58.070 --> 20:59.529
I did save his life earlier--

188
20:59.613 --> 21:01.239
You're going to see my father?

189
21:02.699 --> 21:03.784
Your father?

190
21:04.868 --> 21:07.120
Father, stay inside!

191
21:08.622 --> 21:12.209
Yes, your father. Let's go talk to him together.

192
21:12.292 --> 21:15.295
Let's tell him you're treating me like I'm a pickpocket.

193
21:15.379 --> 21:18.256
He seemed like a fair and reasonable man. Then surely…

194
21:20.592 --> 21:22.010
What do you even know?

195
21:23.136 --> 21:23.970
Excuse me?

196
21:37.734 --> 21:40.278
This is a waste of time. Let's stop arguing.

197
21:40.362 --> 21:43.281
I won't ask who you really are anymore.

198
21:43.365 --> 21:44.699
Just give me back what's in my wallet.

199
21:46.076 --> 21:47.744
You can keep the wallet and the money.

200
21:47.828 --> 21:49.204
I'll let this all go.

201
21:50.455 --> 21:51.706
What's in the wallet?

202
21:55.127 --> 21:56.044
Not worth a thing.

203
21:59.965 --> 22:00.924
Look.

204
22:01.716 --> 22:04.386
You keep going on about your wallet,

205
22:04.469 --> 22:07.514
but I honestly have no idea what you're talking about.

206
22:09.057 --> 22:11.017
This is rather strange.

207
22:11.101 --> 22:14.563
If you're so sure I stole your wallet,

208
22:14.646 --> 22:17.315
why not take me to the police?

209
22:20.694 --> 22:24.531
I suppose you don't want anyone finding out what's in your wallet.

210
22:24.614 --> 22:27.826
Whatever it is, it's useless to you.

211
22:28.577 --> 22:30.704
I'll let you keep the wallet and money.

212
22:30.787 --> 22:32.289
Why do you keep denying you have it?

213
22:32.372 --> 22:34.207
I'm not denying anything.

214
22:34.291 --> 22:36.168
I really don't know.

215
22:40.797 --> 22:44.342
If I hadn't helped you earlier, you'd have been taken for an accomplice.

216
22:46.595 --> 22:48.555
Yet you don't seem grateful at all.

217
22:48.638 --> 22:51.141
You could say the same about yourself.

218
22:51.224 --> 22:53.560
You would've died if it weren't for me, right?

219
22:53.643 --> 22:55.812
Yet here you are, calling your lifesaver a thief--

220
22:55.896 --> 22:57.022
Excuse me.

221
22:57.105 --> 22:58.148
Seo-hee!

222
22:59.691 --> 23:00.650
Seo-hee!

223
23:01.818 --> 23:02.652
Yes, sir!

224
23:02.736 --> 23:04.362
What are you doing there?

225
23:04.446 --> 23:05.280
Come on.

226
23:10.202 --> 23:11.786
Yes, I'm coming.

227
23:17.042 --> 23:18.335
-Let's go. -Okay.

228
23:40.941 --> 23:42.359
I didn't know you were here, Hideo.

229
23:43.318 --> 23:44.569
Are you going somewhere?

230
23:44.653 --> 23:47.781
Yes, my wife's not feeling well, so I called a cab.

231
23:47.864 --> 23:49.324
Excuse me, but I have to run.

232
23:53.119 --> 23:55.121
Go to the Imperial University Affiliated Clinic.

233
24:19.229 --> 24:21.815
I saw you with Sato Hideo outside, so I called you over.

234
24:21.898 --> 24:23.358
What were you talking about with him?

235
24:23.984 --> 24:24.985
Sato Hi…

236
24:27.112 --> 24:28.196
Sato Hideo?

237
24:28.738 --> 24:29.656
Well…

238
25:39.434 --> 25:40.435
You can't come in.

239
25:42.354 --> 25:43.730
Please wait outside.

240
25:47.734 --> 25:49.361
When did the bleeding start?

241
25:50.904 --> 25:53.198
Dr. Kim, I've got her.

242
25:53.281 --> 25:56.034
I'll call if I need you. Go help with the gunshot patient.

243
25:56.117 --> 25:56.993
Okay.

244
26:02.082 --> 26:03.625
What happened?

245
26:03.708 --> 26:05.460
Suzuki was brought in with a gunshot wound.

246
26:05.543 --> 26:06.586
He's in surgery now.

247
26:07.545 --> 26:09.339
We failed.

248
26:10.924 --> 26:13.927
There was someone else with the same goal as us.

249
26:14.469 --> 26:17.138
He shot at Sato before I could.

250
26:17.889 --> 26:20.975
He fled after getting into a shootout with Sato's son.

251
26:23.228 --> 26:25.605
For now, we're in the clear,

252
26:25.689 --> 26:27.607
but not entirely.

253
26:27.691 --> 26:29.984
So let's say I miscarried because of the shooting.

254
26:30.568 --> 26:31.528
We told Sato's son

255
26:31.611 --> 26:33.571
we'd rushed here.

256
26:34.114 --> 26:36.408
Sato will probably want to check tomorrow.

257
26:36.991 --> 26:38.159
Understood.

258
26:40.745 --> 26:41.955
Did you get shot?

259
26:42.038 --> 26:43.331
No.

260
26:43.415 --> 26:45.625
I figured people would notice me coming and going,

261
26:45.709 --> 26:47.335
so I gave myself a little cut.

262
26:47.419 --> 26:48.336
Let me take a look.

263
26:50.380 --> 26:51.881
I'll clean the wound. Bear with me.

264
26:56.136 --> 26:58.513
Who's the woman you came with?

265
27:08.690 --> 27:09.566
Well…

266
27:10.442 --> 27:12.026
She'll be all right, won't she?

267
27:26.291 --> 27:28.626
We couldn't save the baby.

268
27:29.836 --> 27:30.754
I'm sorry.

269
27:31.588 --> 27:35.091
She'll recover after some rest.

270
28:07.123 --> 28:09.542
Yes, Your Excellency, Governor-General!

271
28:12.754 --> 28:13.922
Yes, sir.

272
28:14.005 --> 28:15.715
The American reporter is unharmed.

273
28:15.799 --> 28:17.884
Didn't I make it clear already?

274
28:17.967 --> 28:19.844
We must not let the American reporter

275
28:19.928 --> 28:22.555
detect even a hint of unrest in Joseon.

276
28:22.639 --> 28:24.599
Our priority at the Government-General

277
28:24.682 --> 28:27.644
is getting the League of Nations Commission

278
28:27.727 --> 28:34.609
currently in China to recognize Manchukuo as a legitimate independent state.

279
28:34.692 --> 28:38.696
We must show the world that Manchukuo can become

280
28:38.780 --> 28:42.617
as peaceful as Joseon under Japanese rule.

281
28:42.700 --> 28:44.035
Is that clear?

282
28:44.118 --> 28:45.453
Yes, sir!

283
28:59.509 --> 29:00.343
Father.

284
29:02.053 --> 29:05.723
Mr. Yoo's wife was rushed to the hospital with bleeding.

285
29:19.237 --> 29:22.073
She's quite ill, so please keep a close eye on her.

286
29:22.156 --> 29:23.992
Let me know right away if anything happens.

287
29:24.909 --> 29:26.911
I'm putting together your 100 won.

288
29:27.662 --> 29:29.706
Stay here tonight. I'll pay you tomorrow.

289
29:31.332 --> 29:32.166
Okay.

290
29:35.420 --> 29:36.504
Let me help you.

291
29:36.588 --> 29:38.256
No, it's okay.

292
29:39.924 --> 29:42.260
Honey, help me get changed.

293
29:43.928 --> 29:44.762
Careful.

294
31:18.022 --> 31:20.692
Are you sure you weren't hurt anywhere else?

295
31:21.526 --> 31:22.735
Yeah, I'm fine.

296
31:23.653 --> 31:25.071
This is just a little graze.

297
31:27.073 --> 31:28.032
All done.

298
31:31.869 --> 31:32.954
Thank you.

299
31:35.081 --> 31:37.041
It's late. You should go to bed.

300
31:37.125 --> 31:39.711
It's way past your bedtime.

301
31:39.794 --> 31:42.422
No, I don't want to go to bed.

302
31:42.505 --> 31:43.673
Don't push me.

303
31:43.756 --> 31:45.508
I said don't push me.

304
31:45.591 --> 31:46.759
Good night.

305
31:47.677 --> 31:48.553
Good night.

306
31:48.636 --> 31:50.013
I hate you, Ms. Yanagi.

307
31:50.096 --> 31:51.597
You're the worst!

308
31:51.681 --> 31:53.683
I hate you.

309
31:54.267 --> 31:55.476
Good night, Hanako.

310
31:55.560 --> 31:56.978
Hideo!

311
32:10.742 --> 32:12.326
Father! Are you all right?

312
32:15.663 --> 32:17.790
Father!

313
32:18.458 --> 32:20.376
Mother's gone. Mother…

314
32:22.712 --> 32:23.880
Father…

315
32:25.673 --> 32:26.966
It's me.

316
32:29.385 --> 32:30.762
Hideo.

317
32:35.725 --> 32:37.101
What is it?

318
32:38.895 --> 32:39.979
Mother…

319
32:41.314 --> 32:42.732
She left home.

320
32:44.233 --> 32:45.443
Is…

321
32:46.027 --> 32:48.863
Is that true, Father?

322
34:19.996 --> 34:21.038
Are you up?

323
34:35.595 --> 34:38.306
Still haven't caught him yet? Are you serious right now?

324
34:39.223 --> 34:41.601
We're drawing up a sketch now.

325
34:46.314 --> 34:47.857
Get going now.

326
34:49.317 --> 34:50.318
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir.

327
34:51.360 --> 34:52.278
And you.

328
34:54.488 --> 34:55.990
Who did you say showed up in Keijo?

329
34:56.073 --> 34:59.785
Han Cheol-yong, a key member of the Gugukdan.

330
34:59.869 --> 35:01.037
Han Cheol-yong?

331
35:02.580 --> 35:03.456
Is that confirmed?

332
35:04.665 --> 35:05.666
Yes, sir.

333
35:05.750 --> 35:09.086
He was behind the attempted assassination of the Jongno police chief 12 years ago.

334
35:09.170 --> 35:11.797
He was released two years ago and went to Shanghai.

335
35:11.881 --> 35:14.759
Then he was spotted in Jongno three days ago.

336
35:14.842 --> 35:18.095
The police inspector who'd interrogated him before saw him.

337
35:19.680 --> 35:21.307
Bring me his surveillance card.

338
35:29.148 --> 35:31.400
NAME HAN CHEOL-YONG

339
35:34.111 --> 35:35.821
Gugukdan, is it?

340
35:38.783 --> 35:40.368
Were you with the Gugukdan?

341
35:42.745 --> 35:45.081
How long did you think you could hide it?

342
35:48.626 --> 35:49.752
Gugukdan.

343
35:51.170 --> 35:52.922
I haven't heard that name in a while.

344
35:54.507 --> 35:56.968
Could this be some kind of fate?

345
35:57.551 --> 35:58.719
Sorry?

346
35:59.303 --> 36:03.432
I'll report to the governor-general that the Gugukdan was behind the attack.

347
36:03.516 --> 36:06.978
But that's still just speculation.

348
36:07.061 --> 36:10.690
We won't know for sure if it really was the Gugukdan until we arrest him.

349
36:10.773 --> 36:14.193
It doesn't matter anymore who they really were yesterday.

350
36:14.944 --> 36:17.071
We'll just pin it on the Gugukdan.

351
36:17.863 --> 36:20.074
They've been a thorn in our side for years.

352
36:20.157 --> 36:22.535
We'll use this chance to wipe them out.

353
36:24.245 --> 36:25.288
Is that clear?

354
36:25.997 --> 36:26.831
Yes, sir!

355
36:43.097 --> 36:44.307
Come in.

356
36:55.526 --> 36:57.069
She's not coming back.

357
36:57.737 --> 36:59.739
She was with Sato Hideo last night.

358
36:59.822 --> 37:01.407
That doesn't sit right with me.

359
37:01.490 --> 37:03.409
Could she have gone to him to betray us--

360
37:08.414 --> 37:10.082
The streetcar took forever to come.

361
37:16.255 --> 37:17.089
Here.

362
37:20.301 --> 37:24.722
I brought you some seaweed and a little beef.

363
37:26.849 --> 37:28.559
I hope you get well.

364
37:44.408 --> 37:45.618
Here's the 100 won I promised.

365
37:51.165 --> 37:52.708
Open it and check the amount.

366
37:54.919 --> 37:58.172
It's fine. You wouldn't shortchange someone who nearly died.

367
37:58.839 --> 38:00.925
All right. Then let's part ways here.

368
38:01.592 --> 38:04.428
We'll say you quit because you were scared off by last night.

369
38:05.012 --> 38:07.473
Fine. I'll be going then.

370
38:16.607 --> 38:17.942
Actually, no.

371
38:18.025 --> 38:20.444
I'll just take enough for the beef and seaweed.

372
38:29.328 --> 38:31.539
I don't think we should see each other again.

373
38:31.622 --> 38:35.668
So I won't give back what's in your bag.

374
38:35.751 --> 38:36.794
Fine.

375
38:37.628 --> 38:38.921
Let's not see each other again.

376
38:55.312 --> 38:57.648
I don't think we should let her go like this.

377
38:58.274 --> 39:00.651
She seems to be quite loyal. It should be fine.

378
39:00.734 --> 39:04.280
Our mission fell apart because of her greed for money.

379
39:04.363 --> 39:06.073
So we should tell our comrades--

380
39:06.157 --> 39:07.533
Do you want to get rid of her?

381
39:10.703 --> 39:12.163
That's not like you,

382
39:12.246 --> 39:14.039
to think about hurting someone.

383
39:14.123 --> 39:18.252
Your safety matters more to me than anything, more than anyone else's life.

384
39:27.428 --> 39:28.762
I just hope…

385
39:30.639 --> 39:32.725
you never have to kill anyone.

386
39:33.517 --> 39:34.602
No matter who they are.

387
39:34.685 --> 39:36.937
Even if it's for independence,

388
39:37.438 --> 39:39.106
I don't want you to ever do that.

389
39:43.068 --> 39:45.446
I've always wanted to tell you this.

390
39:46.947 --> 39:50.701
And since I survived, I finally have the chance.

391
39:50.784 --> 39:51.744
Please, promise me.

392
39:54.330 --> 39:56.081
Don't pick up a gun.

393
40:06.050 --> 40:09.261
We promised in Shanghai.

394
40:10.804 --> 40:12.014
Leave the guns to me.

395
40:12.681 --> 40:14.099
That's our job.

396
40:14.934 --> 40:17.269
You use your pen and your words.

397
40:18.062 --> 40:21.982
Tell the world how Japan stole Joseon's sovereignty and committed atrocities.

398
40:24.360 --> 40:26.445
We'll handle the guns and bombs.

399
40:28.113 --> 40:29.114
As for you,

400
40:29.782 --> 40:33.035
once we kill Sato, let the world know what happened.

401
40:37.706 --> 40:39.166
Even though I'm your husband,

402
40:39.250 --> 40:41.919
I'm still not part of the "us" you're talking about.

403
40:52.346 --> 40:55.099
Even if she comes back asking for money,

404
40:55.891 --> 40:59.186
I'll have already killed Sato and be gone by then.

405
41:14.368 --> 41:15.452
Where did it go?

406
41:16.787 --> 41:18.080
I know I tossed it here.

407
41:21.792 --> 41:25.296
Kkot-nim, you barely ate. Why are you going to the outhouse so often?

408
41:25.963 --> 41:27.965
Because my tummy hurts.

409
41:28.048 --> 41:28.924
Hey, No-ma!

410
41:29.008 --> 41:30.342
You scared me.

411
41:30.426 --> 41:31.802
-Ga-kyung. -Hey.

412
41:31.885 --> 41:34.513
Did you see that here?

413
41:34.597 --> 41:35.639
That…

414
41:36.265 --> 41:38.017
That? What's that?

415
41:38.100 --> 41:39.893
Hey, why'd you bring the tissue box?

416
41:39.977 --> 41:42.062
What was it called? That…

417
41:43.063 --> 41:45.566
Right, Lee Ga-kyung. Where'd you sleep last night?

418
41:45.649 --> 41:46.984
We were worried all night.

419
41:47.067 --> 41:51.030
We thought you'd gone to America without telling us.

420
41:51.614 --> 41:52.489
No.

421
41:52.573 --> 41:54.658
I can't afford to go to America yet.

422
41:54.742 --> 41:57.119
That's not important. Did you…

423
41:57.202 --> 41:58.495
not see a piece of paper?

424
41:59.079 --> 42:00.289
What paper?

425
42:00.372 --> 42:02.458
That… pawn ticket!

426
42:02.541 --> 42:04.793
You know, the pawn ticket I found in the wallet I stole.

427
42:04.877 --> 42:06.086
I threw it in here.

428
42:06.170 --> 42:08.172
But I can't find it. Where did it go?

429
42:11.675 --> 42:14.553
Where are you coming back from?

430
42:14.637 --> 42:16.096
The outhouse.

431
42:16.180 --> 42:18.140
Kkot-nim finally had to go after five days.

432
42:18.223 --> 42:19.058
What?

433
42:20.809 --> 42:21.769
Kkot-nim.

434
42:22.728 --> 42:26.106
Did you take the paper from here?

435
42:26.607 --> 42:28.651
You didn't, right? Please say you didn't.

436
42:31.278 --> 42:33.197
If not here, where else would she get it?

437
42:36.158 --> 42:37.534
Oh, no!

438
42:38.035 --> 42:40.120
That's what my life depends on.

439
42:40.204 --> 42:41.080
Your life?

440
42:41.163 --> 42:42.831
Hey, what are you talking about?

441
42:42.915 --> 42:44.917
Hey, you're constipated.

442
42:45.000 --> 42:47.127
Of all days, why today?

443
42:47.920 --> 42:49.254
What am I supposed to do?

444
42:51.840 --> 42:53.300
I've got to do something.

445
42:54.510 --> 42:56.011
I have to get it out. Hold on.

446
42:56.095 --> 42:58.180
Ga-kyung, the thing is…

447
42:58.263 --> 42:59.807
Not now. I'm busy.

448
43:00.516 --> 43:02.768
I didn't poop today.

449
43:07.481 --> 43:08.357
Give me that.

450
43:15.614 --> 43:16.615
Thank goodness.

451
43:21.036 --> 43:22.329
Good girl, Kkot-nim.

452
43:25.541 --> 43:27.418
"Sin Tae-jin."

453
43:28.043 --> 43:30.504
"1919."

454
43:30.587 --> 43:31.463
SIN TAE-JIN

455
43:31.547 --> 43:35.175
Who's Sin Tae-jin? What did he leave at the pawnshop?

456
43:36.885 --> 43:38.429
Is it that important?

457
43:42.808 --> 43:43.642
No way.

458
43:43.726 --> 43:44.977
I'm never giving it back.

459
43:45.060 --> 43:48.397
This is my lifeline until I go to America.

460
43:57.823 --> 43:59.324
ONE WON

461
44:01.410 --> 44:05.038
I nearly died because of those people.

462
44:05.122 --> 44:07.207
Maybe I should've taken the entire 100 won.

463
44:08.208 --> 44:10.961
I've waited so long for this day.

464
44:11.044 --> 44:12.171
You just…

465
44:12.755 --> 44:15.758
destroyed everything I've ever lived for!

466
44:19.720 --> 44:20.971
Forget it.

467
44:21.054 --> 44:23.849
Why get mixed up with dangerous people over 100 won?

468
44:23.932 --> 44:25.267
It does me no good.

469
44:26.101 --> 44:27.936
I absolutely cannot die.

470
44:28.687 --> 44:32.816
I'm going to survive and make it to America.

471
44:36.195 --> 44:39.031
Interpreter Suzuki has been placed on sick leave.

472
44:39.114 --> 44:43.118
But we can't leave the interpreter's post vacant for long.

473
44:44.286 --> 44:45.329
For the time being,

474
44:45.412 --> 44:47.831
you'll serve as a temporary English interpreter.

475
44:47.915 --> 44:49.458
Yes, sir.

476
44:49.541 --> 44:50.793
Because of Manchukuo,

477
44:50.876 --> 44:53.587
we need to manage the foreign press now more than ever.

478
44:54.505 --> 44:56.298
As an English interpreter,

479
44:56.381 --> 44:59.051
make sure to manage the Western journalists well.

480
45:00.219 --> 45:02.554
Both Tokyo and His Excellency the governor-general

481
45:02.638 --> 45:04.139
have their eyes on it.

482
45:05.224 --> 45:06.058
Yes, sir.

483
45:06.141 --> 45:08.977
Pay particular attention to Yoo Philip.

484
45:10.020 --> 45:11.939
I heard his wife was discharged this morning.

485
45:12.022 --> 45:14.191
Go in my stead and offer her my sympathies.

486
45:14.733 --> 45:17.110
He's American, but he's of Joseon descent,

487
45:17.694 --> 45:20.864
so I've been keeping a close eye on him.

488
45:21.490 --> 45:22.825
Then yesterday happened.

489
45:23.867 --> 45:25.828
Even if he did shoot the killer,

490
45:25.911 --> 45:27.287
don't let your guard down.

491
45:27.871 --> 45:30.249
The fact that he had a gun feels off.

492
45:31.250 --> 45:32.292
I…

493
45:33.252 --> 45:35.504
I don't trust Josenjing.

494
45:43.887 --> 45:44.930
Do you trust me?

495
45:49.977 --> 45:52.187
You're my son, Sato Hideo.

496
45:53.647 --> 45:55.899
Then why did you point a gun at me?

497
46:02.030 --> 46:03.824
The day Mother left us…

498
46:07.327 --> 46:09.371
you pointed a gun at me.

499
46:11.623 --> 46:12.583
Why on earth…

500
46:16.211 --> 46:18.380
I wondered why, but I never asked.

501
46:19.006 --> 46:21.550
Instead, I tried to be a son you could be proud of.

502
46:23.677 --> 46:25.512
I tried desperately to prove myself.

503
46:27.431 --> 46:29.474
I was afraid you'd abandon me too.

504
46:32.644 --> 46:33.770
I was afraid…

505
46:34.646 --> 46:36.523
I'd be left alone again.

506
46:41.194 --> 46:43.989
And yet you pointed a gun at me again.

507
46:45.073 --> 46:46.867
Now I want to know why.

508
46:50.495 --> 46:51.872
What do I have to do…

509
46:53.916 --> 46:55.918
to be your son?

510
46:57.169 --> 46:58.086
Tell me.

511
47:03.508 --> 47:04.426
Hideo.

512
47:09.973 --> 47:11.350
Do you have anything else to say?

513
47:14.686 --> 47:16.271
No, Father.

514
47:33.872 --> 47:35.415
So-ran.

515
47:41.463 --> 47:42.339
Give it to me.

516
47:48.887 --> 47:50.138
I'll clean up the house.

517
47:50.222 --> 47:52.474
Forget everything for today and get some rest.

518
47:53.225 --> 47:54.267
No.

519
47:55.102 --> 48:00.148
I need to keep myself busy to forget all these thoughts for a while.

520
48:13.453 --> 48:14.830
About Seo-hee.

521
48:18.333 --> 48:20.460
The name I called her.

522
48:22.504 --> 48:23.422
Keum Seo-hee.

523
48:28.468 --> 48:29.511
Seo-hee…

524
48:31.763 --> 48:33.807
was my daughter's name.

525
48:38.520 --> 48:40.397
March 1st, 1919.

526
48:43.442 --> 48:45.485
Not long after the March 1st Movement,

527
48:46.194 --> 48:50.449
I heard the Japanese were burning villages in retaliation.

528
48:52.117 --> 48:55.287
But I didn't think our village would be one of them.

529
48:56.079 --> 48:56.997
And then…

530
48:57.664 --> 48:58.874
What's going on?

531
48:59.624 --> 49:01.835
No. Please, no. No!

532
49:02.669 --> 49:03.503
No!

533
49:03.587 --> 49:05.714
Please, no! Don't!

534
49:08.300 --> 49:09.509
It's okay, sweetie.

535
49:12.012 --> 49:14.014
Honey.

536
49:15.015 --> 49:17.684
Seok-jung, what's going on? Why are they doing this?

537
49:21.313 --> 49:23.356
My wife and daughter have nothing to do with it.

538
49:24.316 --> 49:25.317
Please let them go.

539
49:25.942 --> 49:28.195
Yes, there must be some misunderstanding.

540
49:28.278 --> 49:31.239
My husband is just a schoolteacher.

541
49:31.323 --> 49:33.366
My family has nothing to do with it.

542
49:33.909 --> 49:35.035
Let them go now.

543
49:35.118 --> 49:36.578
Shut up!

544
49:58.600 --> 49:59.684
Let me ask you again.

545
50:00.727 --> 50:04.314
Tell me who joined you in leading the March 1st protest in this village.

546
50:05.857 --> 50:06.858
Otherwise…

547
50:17.828 --> 50:19.037
I'll kill your daughter.

548
50:22.207 --> 50:23.125
It's the daughter.

549
50:23.708 --> 50:24.751
No.

550
50:24.835 --> 50:25.877
No, please! Don't.

551
50:29.840 --> 50:31.133
Please, don't.

552
50:31.216 --> 50:33.593
No! Kill me, not her.

553
50:33.677 --> 50:35.595
Not my daughter. Please.

554
50:35.679 --> 50:37.472
Please, I'm begging you.

555
50:37.556 --> 50:38.598
Seok-jung.

556
50:38.682 --> 50:41.643
Honey, tell them something, honey.

557
50:41.726 --> 50:42.853
Honey.

558
50:42.936 --> 50:45.438
How many times did I tell you? I did it by myself.

559
50:45.522 --> 50:47.399
The protest in this village

560
50:49.025 --> 50:49.943
was all me.

561
50:50.902 --> 50:52.112
I planned it all myself.

562
50:52.195 --> 50:53.113
Tell me.

563
50:53.864 --> 50:54.948
Who's your accomplice?

564
50:55.031 --> 50:55.907
Honey…

565
50:56.658 --> 50:58.160
Seok-jung!

566
50:59.536 --> 51:01.496
I swear, I did it alone.

567
51:12.966 --> 51:13.800
Shoot.

568
51:15.510 --> 51:16.595
No!

569
51:36.531 --> 51:37.490
Let go!

570
51:54.132 --> 51:56.218
This is your last chance.

571
51:56.301 --> 51:58.178
Tell me who else was involved.

572
51:58.720 --> 51:59.888
This time,

573
52:00.722 --> 52:01.556
it's your wife.

574
52:06.394 --> 52:07.437
I'm sorry.

575
52:12.567 --> 52:13.860
Na Byeong-sun,

576
52:16.321 --> 52:17.739
Choi Man-chun,

577
52:19.115 --> 52:20.825
and Kim Pung-san.

578
52:24.913 --> 52:26.206
Only three?

579
52:27.749 --> 52:28.667
Yes.

580
52:30.001 --> 52:31.378
Now, keep your word…

581
52:31.461 --> 52:32.545
Set it on fire.

582
52:32.629 --> 52:33.797
Set it on fire!

583
52:55.151 --> 52:56.444
No!

584
52:57.696 --> 52:59.447
This isn't what you promised.

585
53:00.532 --> 53:03.034
Those people are all innocent.

586
53:03.618 --> 53:06.329
Please, please, put out the fire.

587
53:06.913 --> 53:07.872
Please.

588
53:12.460 --> 53:15.880
I don't think I said I'd spare them.

589
53:25.140 --> 53:27.767
You damn monster!

590
53:28.643 --> 53:30.603
What did we ever do to deserve this?

591
53:32.439 --> 53:35.025
We only asked for our country back.

592
53:35.108 --> 53:37.694
We only cried out for independence!

593
53:38.361 --> 53:39.863
But you people…

594
53:39.946 --> 53:41.197
Take him away!

595
53:41.698 --> 53:44.117
You worthless bastards!

596
54:14.731 --> 54:16.691
No!

597
55:39.399 --> 55:41.943
We had our daughter after ten years of marriage,

598
55:42.986 --> 55:44.654
and that's how I lost her.

599
55:48.575 --> 55:51.119
I never went to school. I couldn't even read or write.

600
55:51.202 --> 55:53.538
My husband and daughter were all I had.

601
55:53.621 --> 55:55.498
I was just a country woman,

602
55:56.916 --> 55:58.293
but that day

603
55:59.127 --> 56:01.129
completely changed my life.

604
57:07.111 --> 57:08.029
I'd once heard

605
57:08.988 --> 57:12.909
there was a place called Gugukdan in Shanghai.

606
57:14.577 --> 57:17.288
So I made my way there, risking my life time and again,

607
57:17.372 --> 57:20.375
crossing mountains, fields, and rivers.

608
57:34.806 --> 57:36.933
A LIBERATED HOMELAND

609
57:43.106 --> 57:44.607
INDEPENDENCE FOR KOREA

610
57:54.325 --> 57:55.326
I want to kill…

611
58:00.373 --> 58:02.500
that bastard.

612
58:20.184 --> 58:22.270
I learned how to fire a gun.

613
58:22.353 --> 58:23.563
I was determined

614
58:23.646 --> 58:26.107
to be the one to kill him with my own hands.

615
59:02.602 --> 59:03.519
This way.

616
59:30.129 --> 59:33.466
I never imagined it'd take this long to find him

617
59:34.008 --> 59:36.928
after he returned to Japan.

618
59:38.680 --> 59:41.099
When I heard he was coming back to Joseon,

619
59:42.850 --> 59:44.977
I cried until I had no tears left.

620
59:47.647 --> 59:49.399
Finally, my chance had come.

621
59:50.400 --> 59:51.442
But then…

622
59:53.152 --> 59:56.614
For 13 years, I didn't know if he was alive or dead.

623
59:56.698 --> 01:00:00.535
The man I'd sworn to kill if we ever crossed paths again.

624
01:00:01.911 --> 01:00:02.995
It was my husband.

625
01:00:04.956 --> 01:00:08.793
In that moment, when I had to call her something…

626
01:00:08.876 --> 01:00:09.919
Keum Seo-hee!

627
01:00:11.838 --> 01:00:15.591
I called her Seo-hee.

628
01:00:23.307 --> 01:00:25.268
For 13 years,

629
01:00:25.351 --> 01:00:29.021
I'd never spoken that name aloud.

630
01:00:34.026 --> 01:00:35.069
Seo-hee.

631
01:00:37.447 --> 01:00:39.991
I'd said that name thousands of times a day.

632
01:00:42.034 --> 01:00:44.078
I suppose it just came out.

633
01:00:54.964 --> 01:00:56.591
In Shanghai,

634
01:00:58.801 --> 01:01:02.013
every year on my daughter's birthday, I managed to find seaweed

635
01:01:02.513 --> 01:01:05.057
and made a bowl of seaweed soup.

636
01:01:11.898 --> 01:01:13.107
I don't think

637
01:01:15.401 --> 01:01:17.111
I could ever eat that.

638
01:01:56.108 --> 01:01:57.610
You didn't have to bring this.

639
01:01:58.528 --> 01:02:00.530
I hope your wife recovers well.

640
01:02:01.864 --> 01:02:03.741
I was deeply sorry to hear the news.

641
01:02:03.825 --> 01:02:05.201
My father also asked me to offer

642
01:02:05.701 --> 01:02:08.079
his deepest sympathy and condolences.

643
01:02:08.663 --> 01:02:09.914
Thank you.

644
01:02:12.333 --> 01:02:14.502
My wife is asleep after taking some medicine.

645
01:02:20.216 --> 01:02:22.426
Sorry things are a little messy.

646
01:02:23.010 --> 01:02:25.096
I hope you'll understand.

647
01:02:25.179 --> 01:02:26.597
We only just got back.

648
01:02:29.600 --> 01:02:31.018
Last night must've been shocking.

649
01:02:32.311 --> 01:02:34.146
I'm sure you were both shaken.

650
01:02:36.148 --> 01:02:38.860
As I promised, I didn't run a story about last night.

651
01:02:39.944 --> 01:02:40.820
Thank you.

652
01:02:47.577 --> 01:02:49.495
Is your maid all right?

653
01:02:51.747 --> 01:02:52.790
The maid…

654
01:02:52.874 --> 01:02:53.708
Oh, you mean Seo-hee?

655
01:02:54.959 --> 01:02:56.127
Yes.

656
01:02:56.210 --> 01:02:57.753
It seems like she's not here.

657
01:02:57.837 --> 01:02:59.672
Did she go out on an errand?

658
01:03:00.506 --> 01:03:02.925
I'm afraid she quit.

659
01:03:04.844 --> 01:03:05.678
She quit?

660
01:03:05.761 --> 01:03:07.972
I think she was shaken by what happened yesterday.

661
01:03:09.390 --> 01:03:11.475
She's never seen a gun or blood before.

662
01:03:11.559 --> 01:03:13.895
I tried to convince her, but she wouldn't change her mind.

663
01:03:16.063 --> 01:03:18.190
Yes, that's no surprise. I understand.

664
01:03:24.989 --> 01:03:26.782
Do you know where she lives?

665
01:03:27.909 --> 01:03:28.743
Her home?

666
01:03:29.827 --> 01:03:31.454
No, I don't. Why do you ask?

667
01:03:32.079 --> 01:03:35.416
If it weren't for her, something terrible could've happened to my father.

668
01:03:36.000 --> 01:03:38.127
I wanted to thank her, at least.

669
01:03:39.545 --> 01:03:40.713
It's a shame she's gone.

670
01:03:42.673 --> 01:03:43.925
I appreciate the thought,

671
01:03:44.008 --> 01:03:46.427
but there's really no need to go to such lengths.

672
01:03:47.303 --> 01:03:48.346
Very well.

673
01:03:56.103 --> 01:03:57.730
I'll see you later.

674
01:03:59.023 --> 01:04:00.107
Okay. Take care.

675
01:04:16.290 --> 01:04:17.875
They're looking for her.

676
01:04:21.170 --> 01:04:25.675
If I had a million won

677
01:04:26.258 --> 01:04:27.885
I'd save up to go to America

678
01:04:27.969 --> 01:04:29.929
We replaced the filling with cotton.

679
01:04:30.012 --> 01:04:32.098
It should be nice and fluffy.

680
01:04:32.974 --> 01:04:35.476
I'll ring the bell ten minutes before your two hours are up.

681
01:04:35.559 --> 01:04:36.894
If you want to stay longer,

682
01:04:36.978 --> 01:04:39.605
just pull this cord on the wall.

683
01:04:40.815 --> 01:04:41.941
And I'd buy…

684
01:04:42.024 --> 01:04:43.484
Hang on. What time is it?

685
01:04:43.567 --> 01:04:44.402
Damn it.

686
01:04:44.485 --> 01:04:46.237
FIVE, FOUR, THREE, TWO, ONE

687
01:04:47.071 --> 01:04:48.698
They're always running over.

688
01:04:48.781 --> 01:04:49.740
Mister.

689
01:04:49.824 --> 01:04:52.326
You charge one won for a whole night.

690
01:04:52.410 --> 01:04:55.705
Isn't 50 jeon for two hours during the day a bit much?

691
01:04:56.330 --> 01:04:58.290
You're really going to get rich.

692
01:04:58.374 --> 01:05:00.376
Now you realize that?

693
01:05:01.836 --> 01:05:03.337
That's why, Ga-kyung,

694
01:05:03.421 --> 01:05:06.716
if you marry me, this pawnshop and inn will all be yours.

695
01:05:06.799 --> 01:05:09.051
Wasn't it your youngest's 100th day yesterday?

696
01:05:09.135 --> 01:05:10.469
Not yesterday. The day before.

697
01:05:10.553 --> 01:05:13.472
Hey, if you bring your boyfriend,

698
01:05:13.556 --> 01:05:15.599
I'll make it 30 jeon just for you.

699
01:05:15.683 --> 01:05:16.851
Come on.

700
01:05:16.934 --> 01:05:20.062
We've known each other for so long. Can't you do better than 30?

701
01:05:20.146 --> 01:05:22.606
Other places are begging me to come for free.

702
01:05:22.690 --> 01:05:25.067
What? Do you really have someone?

703
01:05:26.193 --> 01:05:27.445
It looks like you do.

704
01:05:27.528 --> 01:05:29.071
Hey, just bring him along.

705
01:05:29.155 --> 01:05:32.158
I'll let you stay the night for free, not just during the day.

706
01:05:32.241 --> 01:05:33.951
You can't take that back.

707
01:05:34.910 --> 01:05:37.455
Just bring the guy here.

708
01:05:37.538 --> 01:05:40.374
Men know men.

709
01:05:41.667 --> 01:05:43.961
Here. This is for the bullets.

710
01:05:45.254 --> 01:05:47.131
All right.

711
01:05:48.549 --> 01:05:50.968
Just marry me, and all this will be yours.

712
01:05:51.052 --> 01:05:52.386
Thank you.

713
01:05:52.470 --> 01:05:55.264
If you find any more, bring them here, not anywhere else.

714
01:05:55.347 --> 01:05:56.265
Okay.

715
01:05:58.142 --> 01:05:59.351
By the way,

716
01:05:59.435 --> 01:06:03.647
do people ever pawn something and not come back for it for 13 years?

717
01:06:03.731 --> 01:06:06.358
Thirteen years? Who would do that?

718
01:06:06.942 --> 01:06:08.652
The interest alone after 13 years

719
01:06:08.736 --> 01:06:12.323
could buy that item back several times over.

720
01:06:12.406 --> 01:06:13.657
Right?

721
01:06:13.741 --> 01:06:16.035
Unless the item meant a lot to them.

722
01:06:16.118 --> 01:06:19.997
If that's the case, wouldn't they come back for it sooner?

723
01:06:20.623 --> 01:06:21.916
I mean

724
01:06:21.999 --> 01:06:25.586
something you wouldn't want anyone to find at home--

725
01:06:25.669 --> 01:06:26.962
Welcome.

726
01:06:27.046 --> 01:06:28.714
-Welcome. -Welcome.

727
01:06:29.340 --> 01:06:30.841
Excuse me.

728
01:06:30.925 --> 01:06:33.511
Have you been running this shop for long?

729
01:06:41.310 --> 01:06:42.269
Oh my.

730
01:06:43.229 --> 01:06:44.230
Hello.

731
01:06:47.024 --> 01:06:48.859
-Over there! -Why? What?

732
01:07:09.630 --> 01:07:10.673
Got you.

733
01:07:11.257 --> 01:07:12.174
The pickpocket.

734
01:07:58.179 --> 01:08:02.099
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

735
01:08:03.017 --> 01:08:05.644
Do you want to send another spy?

736
01:08:05.728 --> 01:08:07.730
I said this is your last chance.

737
01:08:09.982 --> 01:08:12.902
Sin Tae-jin. Does the inspector general know him?

738
01:08:12.985 --> 01:08:14.820
I want to know all of a sudden.

739
01:08:14.904 --> 01:08:16.655
She's sharp and a good liar.

740
01:08:16.739 --> 01:08:17.907
You look so gorgeous.

741
01:08:17.990 --> 01:08:20.576
She's quick on her feet and quick with her hands.

742
01:08:20.659 --> 01:08:22.745
But she'll definitely put us in danger.

743
01:08:23.829 --> 01:08:25.539
Do you want me to be a spy?

744
01:08:25.623 --> 01:08:28.500
You just do what we tell you.

745
01:08:28.584 --> 01:08:30.252
I was wondering…

746
01:08:30.961 --> 01:08:33.255
Why did you come to the Government-General?

747
01:08:39.178 --> 01:08:41.180
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
